  <section class="content-section reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Real-world impact</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mb-12">Sector scenarios & case studies</h2>
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>A GCC government agency deployed a unified command centre to coordinate municipal services, emergency response, and public safety across a metropolitan area serving millions of residents. Siloed agency systems — traffic management, surveillance, environmental sensors, emergency dispatch — produced overlapping data with no correlation. MEAICON built an integration layer that ingested IoT sensor feeds, surveillance camera streams, and incident-management records into a single operational picture, with automated correlation rules that surfaced compound events such as a traffic anomaly near a surveillance gap during a scheduled public gathering. Operators gained situational awareness that previously required manual cross-agency phone calls and spreadsheets.</p>
          <p>In North Africa, a municipal government rolling out a smart-city programme needed to deploy thousands of environmental and utility sensors across urban infrastructure. The sensor fleet produced a data volume that overwhelmed legacy monitoring tools, and unencrypted telemetry transit raised sovereignty concerns. MEAICON implemented a sovereign-hosted IoT platform with encrypted telemetry transport, device identity attestation, and anomaly detection tuned for sensor-tamper and spoofing attacks. The municipality gained reliable, tamper-evident sensor data streams that fed both operational dashboards and national cybersecurity compliance reporting.</p>
          <p>Across East Africa, a regional government consolidated city-wide surveillance and access-control systems following a series of public-safety incidents. Fragmented video management platforms and inconsistent retention policies hampered investigations. MEAICON deployed a unified video surveillance backbone with centralized retention management, role-based access aligned to investigative authority, and automated video analytics that flagged incidents for operator review. The consolidated platform reduced evidence-gathering time from days to hours and established an auditable chain of custody for all footage used in proceedings.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Case study highlight</h3>
          <p>See how MEAICON delivered a unified command centre for a GCC government agency, integrating IoT sensor feeds, surveillance, and incident management with automated correlation.</p>
